# promise: #563
# A page's right-click menu has Arc's rows and no "Open in reading mode". Chrome adds that row (and
# "Listen to this page") to open its reading mode side panel, which on Cra's engine opened in the
# page's hidden Chrome window: the row did nothing (0.1.49). Arc's page menu has no reading mode.
# The menu's rows are read as it opens, then it closes. Arc's menu has "Translate to <language>"
# after Cast… when Chromium offers translation, which needs a Google API key: release builds have
# one, so the run sets a stand-in and the row may show (it did on 0.1.51's release check).
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
env GOOGLE_API_KEY=cra-scenario
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=article
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://debug?menuShown=next
expect-log Cra menu shown: waiting
cra://debug?cdp=Input.dispatchMouseEvent&params={"type":"mousePressed","x":300,"y":300,"button":"right","buttons":2,"clickCount":1}
cra://debug?cdp=Input.dispatchMouseEvent&params={"type":"mouseReleased","x":300,"y":300,"button":"right","buttons":0,"clickCount":1}
expect-log Cra menu shown: Back\|Forward\|Reload\|Save As…\|Print…\|Cast…\|(Translate to [^|]+\|)?View Page Source\|Inspect$
